\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {I}{\ignorespaces The falsifiable run matrix: twenty-seven cells. The sign structure predicts a drifting midpoint for the mixed pair only, reversal under swapping the sectors, and a $d^{-2}$ rate; every control row must be null. $\Delta X$ at $t=200$ unless marked. The separation scan is $d_0=8,12,16,20$; the deeper solve drives the elliptic residual $4.4\times $ further; the AMR cell enables one refinement level; the mass ladder is three retuned pairs; the stability scan covers $\omega =0.75$--$0.90$. Full cell names and per-cell data are in the results pack (Sec.~\ref {sec:repro}).}}{4}{table.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:matrix}{{I}{4}{The falsifiable run matrix: twenty-seven cells. The sign structure predicts a drifting midpoint for the mixed pair only, reversal under swapping the sectors, and a $d^{-2}$ rate; every control row must be null. $\Delta X$ at $t=200$ unless marked. The separation scan is $d_0=8,12,16,20$; the deeper solve drives the elliptic residual $4.4\times $ further; the AMR cell enables one refinement level; the mass ladder is three retuned pairs; the stability scan covers $\omega =0.75$--$0.90$. Full cell names and per-cell data are in the results pack (Sec.~\ref {sec:repro})}{table.1}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {B}Diagnostics and the run matrix}{4}{section*.10}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The runaway in the headline cell (\texttt  {PM}, $d_0=10$, $\Delta x=0.25$), $z=0$ plane, at $t=0$, $60$, $120$, $200$. Top: scalar-field activity $\mathcal  {A}=\DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ _s(|\Phi _s|^2+|\Pi _s|^2)^{1/2}$, both sectors, projected. Bottom: $\chi -1$; the phantom star is a \emph  {hill} ($\chi >1$, left) and the canonical star a \emph  {well} ($\chi <1$, right)---the model's one sign, photographed. Open markers: the tracked cores (circle $\Phi _+$, square $\Phi _-$); dashed ticks mark the release positions $x=37$ and $27$, arrows the displacement since release, and the bracketed number is the measured gap. Both stars move toward $+x$ at constant acceleration while the gap holds to $1\%$.}}{5}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:frames}{{3}{5}{The runaway in the headline cell (\texttt {PM}, $d_0=10$, $\Delta x=0.25$), $z=0$ plane, at $t=0$, $60$, $120$, $200$. Top: scalar-field activity $\mathcal {A}=\sum _s(|\Phi _s|^2+|\Pi _s|^2)^{1/2}$, both sectors, projected. Bottom: $\chi -1$; the phantom star is a \emph {hill} ($\chi >1$, left) and the canonical star a \emph {well} ($\chi <1$, right)---the model's one sign, photographed. Open markers: the tracked cores (circle $\Phi _+$, square $\Phi _-$); dashed ticks mark the release positions $x=37$ and $27$, arrows the displacement since release, and the bracketed number is the measured gap. Both stars move toward $+x$ at constant acceleration while the gap holds to $1\%$}{figure.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces (a)~Core worldlines in the headline cell ($\Delta x=0.25$): the phantom chases the canonical star it repels; the gap is marked at three times. (b)~Midpoint drift of the $t=400$ run (solid) with the single constant-acceleration fit over $5\le t\le 400$ (dotted)---one parabola holds for the whole run---and the finest-grid $t\le 200$ cell (dashed). (c)~The signal against every null on a log scale: the mixed pair (barycentre midpoint) against the lone stars (core tracker; the off-centre phantom is the sharper test) and the same-sign pair centroids---a separation of $3$--$4$ orders of magnitude, sustained for the whole run.}}{5}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:traj}{{4}{5}{(a)~Core worldlines in the headline cell ($\Delta x=0.25$): the phantom chases the canonical star it repels; the gap is marked at three times. (b)~Midpoint drift of the $t=400$ run (solid) with the single constant-acceleration fit over $5\le t\le 400$ (dotted)---one parabola holds for the whole run---and the finest-grid $t\le 200$ cell (dashed). (c)~The signal against every null on a log scale: the mixed pair (barycentre midpoint) against the lone stars (core tracker; the off-centre phantom is the sharper test) and the same-sign pair centroids---a separation of $3$--$4$ orders of magnitude, sustained for the whole run}{figure.4}{}}
